-- gab/zaehler.gab -- Brandmauer lane bm4: concurrent packet counters.
--
-- Every worker thread counts through this module: packets seen (GESAMT),
-- per-verdict outcomes (VERWORFEN/DROP, AKZEPTIERT/ACCEPT, ABGEWIESEN/REJECT),
-- malformed packets (FEHLFORM), connection-table-full events (VOLL), per-rule
-- hits (REGEL000 .. REGEL255) and their total (REGELSUMME).
--
-- DESIGN, and why it looks the way it does:
-- * ATOMICS, not a lock. A counter that loses increments under load is a bug
--   the operator sees and cannot explain, so every increment is a bounded
--   compare-exchange loop (`exchange update`), never load/store (`+=` on a
--   shared counter is a load-operate-store sequence and loses updates).
-- * `relaxed`: counters are statistics, a payload-free class (SPRACHE.md). No
--   counter carries a payload, no reader pairs with a writer, so no ordering
--   stronger than relaxed is owed. Losslessness comes from the CAS loop.
-- * WRAPPING at 2^32 (`+% 1` in `folge`), SNMP-style. A saturating counter
--   hides traffic volume once full; a wrapping one stays a rate source.
-- * The `+%` step lives in `folge(x : u32)`, never on the exchange binder or
--   a local: the emitter refuses wrapping arithmetic whose exact ranges it
--   cannot read off a declaration (C001, see messung/BEFUNDE-bm4.md).
-- * The CAS loop is `bounded 64 ops`, exit `zaehler_streit` (diverges): the
--   language forbids an unbounded CAS loop, so the bound and the exit are
--   written at every increment (C001 without them). 64 lost races in a row
--   needs 64 consecutive colliding winners; the abort is the mandated price
--   of boundedness, not an expected event.
-- * 256 scalar atomics, not one atomic array: the checker accepts an indexed
--   atomic, the emitter refuses it (C001, see BEFUNDE). Dispatch is therefore
--   an if/else chain; `match` has no wildcard arm (D2) and no integer arms.
-- * `accumulates` is unusable here: it carries no `pub` (P041) while every
--   exported function naming it in `effects` owes `pub` there (N038).
-- * Each `exchange` binds its old value and the helpers RETURN it; callers
--   discard it as a statement (the emitter writes `(void)f();`). Without the
--   return the emitted binding is set-but-unused and fails cc -Werror.
--
-- ACCOUNTING (caller's discipline, stated here so misuse is visible):
-- * One packet: exactly one `zaehle_urteil` call. GESAMT rises with every
--   verdict, so GESAMT == VERWORFEN + AKZEPTIERT + ABGEWIESEN (mod 2^32).
-- * `zaehle_fehl` / `zaehle_voll` / `zaehle_regel` never touch GESAMT.
-- * `zaehle_regel` rises together with REGELSUMME (one extra CAS loop).
--
-- READING: `lies_zaehler(w)` maps 0 GESAMT, 1 VERWORFEN, 2 AKZEPTIERT,
-- 3 ABGEWIESEN, 4 FEHLFORM, 5 VOLL, 6 REGELSUMME, 7..15 reserved (0).
-- Per-rule values come from `lies_regel_treffer(r)`: 16 addresses cannot
-- name 256 rules.

module brandmauer::zaehler {

